# Load a frozen caster, level him up twice through the ordinary sheet G
# command (Player::AdvanceLevel), take Intensive Study on the second level-up
# (the feat auto-picks its only eligible study, "Improve Caster Level"), and
# photograph the sheet's Spell Slots line before and after. bd inc-ngku: the
# study raising AbilityLevel(CA_SPELLCASTING) must raise Spell Slots to the
# spellcasting chart at the new effective caster level, not leave it at the
# raw class level's slots.
#
# THE CHARACTER. tools/fixtures/chars/prestige-geomancy-seed1-opt0822.sav is
# Ferris, a single-class Bard 7 whose Spellcasting ability sits at 3rd
# (sheet line "Spellcasting (3rd)"), well behind the 4/5-of-character-level
# cap Character::getEligableStudies() (src/Create.cpp:3877) checks, so
# Intensive Study's caster-level study (STUDY_CASTING) is eligible. The
# fixture's settings (options-2026-08-22-freeadv.dat, OPT_FREE_ADV forced to
# 1) leave XP-gated advancement off, so the sheet's G command works without
# any wizard-mode setup -- and the load copies the .sav into the run
# sandbox, so the fixture itself is untouched. The character sheet header
# shows he is already in Wizard Mode from how the fixture was made; that
# only changes which key opens the debug menu (unused here), not gameplay.
#
# THE TWO LEVEL-UPS. Player::AdvanceLevel (src/Create.cpp:2672) grants a
# feat only when the new TotalLevel() is 1 or a multiple of 3
# (src/Create.cpp:2834). Bard 7 -> 8 is not (8%3), so the first G only
# raises the level and offers the attribute-bonus menu because 8%4==0
# (src/Create.cpp:2747) -- @until presses 'a' (Strength) until the sheet's
# Class line shows Bard 8, soaking up that menu and the "You feel stronger"
# message box in one step, the same pattern tools/keys/levelup-caster-sheet.keys
# uses. Bard 8 -> 9 IS a multiple of 3, so the second G calls
# GainFeat(FT_FULL_LIST) and Intensive Study is on that MENU_SORTED list,
# so @choose finds it by name. FT_INTENSIVE_STUDY's own case
# (src/Create.cpp:3143) finds only one eligible study at this point
# (getEligableStudies() has one bit set) and takes it without a further
# "Choose an area to improve:" menu -- confirmed by dumping the raw screen
# right after choosing the feat before adding this line.

@dump:arrival

s               # one real turn (Search, finds nothing), so this counts as a
                # session
@dump:played

d               # character sheet
@expect "Class  Bard 7"
@dump:sheet-before

G               # Bard 7 -> 8: no feat (8%3 != 0); attribute bonus offered
@until "Class  Bard 8" a
@dump:after-level8

G               # Bard 8 -> 9: feat granted (9%3==0)
@choose "Intensive Study"
@dump:sheet-after

ESC             # leave the sheet, back to play mode
@quit
